Patch 12 -- p69 context_apply_draw_state correctness bridge.

Incremental after patch 11 and Wine patches 65--66. Entry 39 carries one pointer
to a guest-stack argument/result object and invokes only
context_apply_draw_state() after the guest has acquired and made the GL context
current. The wrapper reuses the p67 TLS guard and fails closed to the guest body
if that guard is unavailable.

MGS2_P69_CORRECTNESS enables a small exported memory-only record for calls,
FALSE results and guest fallbacks. It adds no stderr output and is intended only
for the first correctness run. Regenerate mgs2_island_entry_identity.h and class
B from the exact paired p69 DLL; the built artifact used for the first run has
entry 39 marker +9 at canonical RVA 0xb8ae0 and 1614 class-B IDs.

No A/B logic is added. If picture correctness passes, a later timing build must
disable this record, draw/frame witnesses, display-lock history and island
diagnostics before adding a symmetric guest-side selector.

